<Shell title="Privacy Notice | TwinPALS" description="How the TwinPALS project website handles page requests, catalogue searches, study replays and email enquiries.">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p>Danny Petschke, based in Sweden, operates the TwinPALS project website and is the data controller for its publication and project correspondence. You can reach him at <a href="mailto:twinpals@proton.me">twinpals@proton.me</a>.</p>

    <h2>When you visit</h2>
    <p>GitHub Pages hosts the public site. Your browser sends GitHub your IP address and requests for the pages and files you open. GitHub logs visitors’ IP addresses for security, including visits from people who are signed out. The operator relies on legitimate interests under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR to make the research software and documentation accessible and to keep the website secure.</p>
    <p>GitHub sets the retention period for its logs according to the purpose and its legal obligations. Its Pages documentation gives no fixed period for visitor IP addresses. GitHub and its service providers may process data outside the European Economic Area, including in the United States. GitHub describes the applicable safeguards, including EU standard contractual clauses and its participation in the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, in its privacy statement.</p>
    <p><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Pages data collection</a> · <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub privacy statement and transfer safeguards</a></p>

    <h2>Cookies and interactive examples</h2>
    <p>The project website sets no cookies and uses no visitor analytics, advertising trackers or third-party embeds. Fonts, images and scripts load from the site itself. Your browser can cache these files.</p>
    <p>Catalogue searches and filters run in your browser. The study replay displays recorded results. Neither sends your input to the project or an AI provider. Selecting “Copy prompt” writes the displayed example to your clipboard. When you follow an external link, such as a software download on GitHub or a journal article, the destination receives your request under its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>If you send an email</h2>
    <p>Contact is optional. If you write, the operator uses your email address, any name you supply and your message to answer your enquiry. The legal basis is the legitimate interest in responding to project correspondence under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Correspondence is kept for as long as needed to resolve the enquiry and any follow-up, or longer if a legal obligation requires it.</p>
    <p>Proton Mail provides the project mailbox. Proton states that it stores mail on servers in Switzerland, Germany or Norway. The European Commission recognises Switzerland as providing adequate protection for personal data.</p>
    <p><a href="https://proton.me/mail/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Proton Mail privacy policy</a> · <a href="https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/international-dimension-data-protection/adequacy-decisions_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">European Commission adequacy decisions</a></p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can request access to your personal data, correction of inaccurate data and, where the legal conditions are met, erasure or restriction of processing. Contact <a href="mailto:twinpals@proton.me">twinpals@proton.me</a> to exercise these rights.</p>
    <p><strong>Right to object.</strong> You can object at any time, for reasons relating to your particular situation, to processing based on legitimate interests.</p>
    <p>You can lodge a complaint with the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY) or with the supervisory authority where you live, work or believe an infringement occurred. <a href="https://www.imy.se/en/individuals/forms-and-e-services/file-a-gdpr-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">File a complaint with IMY</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Shell>
